  "authority": "One figure: what Coates CHARGES, at the 2026 street rate card — fencing is the one thing on this event priced from that card rather than the circuit card, on Andrew Fisher's answer of 19 Sep 2026 — each docket column matched by hand to a card line and named. The card's per-metre rates include transport and install; prices exclude GST and damage waiver. The docket columns and the rows already entered come from the fencing cost tracker prepared by Brenden Meek (North) and supplied by Andrew Fisher on 10 Sep 2026; the tracker's own rate row is carried as cost_rate — what Advanced bill each line at — and the Fencing tab shows it beside the charge as what Coates pays, never added to it (v5.60; off in v5.79 on Andrew Fisher's word of 23 Sep 2026 that fencing shows only what we charge; back on his word of 24 Sep 2026 that fencing shows charged and paid again). The record's own money — the Costs tab, the branches, every total — is the charge; what is committed to the fencing contractor is on its purchase orders. A rate can be typed over on the Fencing tab, per column, on either side, in the typer's name. Andrew Fisher, 19 Sep 2026: fencing at the 2026 rates only. Where the card has no line, or he names the charge himself, the rate is his and carries his name and the date (Labour 22 Sep; Scrim, CCB and CCB Demarc 24 Sep 2026).",
